---
// Trang EN: ABOUT — /en/about/
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Who is behind Mechanical Watch Knowledge — and the editorial standard every article on this site is held to.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <div class="mb-3 h-1 w-12 rounded bg-brass"></div>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl text-navy dark:text-dark-text sm:text-5xl">About</h1>

    <div class="prose-content mt-8">
      <p>
        <strong>Mechanical Watch Knowledge</strong> is the English edition of <em>Kienthucdonghoco.vn</em>
        ("Đồng Hồ Cơ"), a Vietnamese encyclopedia of mechanical watches built on one belief:
        watch knowledge deserves to be explained clearly, sourced properly, and written for the reader —
        whether in Vietnamese or in English.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site is</h2>
      <p>
        A practical, source-led guide to mechanical watches — from first principles to collecting.
        The English launch edition covers the foundations: how a movement works, the terms worth
        knowing, three brands that shaped the industry, and three watches that defined their categories.
      </p>

      <h2>How content is checked</h2>
      <p>The editorial rule fits in one sentence: <strong>better missing than wrong.</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Every date, calibre name and specification must be checkable against a source</strong> — manufacturer pages, the Fondation de la Haute Horlogerie, and edited trade publications first.</li>
        <li><strong>Facts that cannot be verified are left out</strong> — no guessing, no vague phrasing to paper over gaps.</li>
        <li><strong>Sources are listed at the end of every article.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>No prices, no investment advice, no "best of" claims.</strong> Prices date quickly and vary by market; the site describes positioning instead.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>One editor, not a newsroom</h2>
      <p>
        The site is written and maintained by a single editor. That keeps the voice and standard
        consistent — and it means mistakes are possible. <strong>If you spot an error, please report it
        via the Contact page</strong>; it will be checked, corrected, and acknowledged.
      </p>

      <h2>Language</h2>
      <p>
        Vietnamese is the original and primary language of this site — with far more articles, animated
        mechanism explainers and interactive tools than the English launch edition. Use the language
        switch in the header to move between editions; pages without an English translation stay
        Vietnamese-only for now, and the switch will take you to the English home page instead of a dead link.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
